---
import '../styles/single-page/index.css';
import ThemedLayout from '../layouts/ThemedLayout.astro';
import LumeloreLogoInteractive from '../components/LumeloreLogoInteractive.astro';
---

<ThemedLayout title='Lumelore'>
	<LumeloreLogoInteractive size={4} />
	<section>
		<h2>Welcome!</h2>
		<hr/>
		<p>My name is Lumelore. I'm a midwestern trans woman, artist, and game developer. I'm in my early twenties and came into possession of a computer science bachelor's not too long ago. Ever since I was a little kid, I knew that I wanted to make video games. I started off in my tweens making silly little Minecraft mods, and a little while later I starting making silly little games with Scratch. This led to my love of pixel art, which I've been creating for over a decade.</p>

		<p>I made this site myself with my own brains using primarily html & css. There is a minimal amount of javascript for non-essential functions that can't be done otherwise. If you use a script blocker like me, nearly everything should work just fine.</p>

		<p>Thank you for checking out my webbed site! ♡</p>
	</section>
	
	<small><br/><br/>Updates Sept 2026: I am currently experiencing a weird issue with how the violet theme renders sometimes specifically on firefox desktop. Still working on fixing that. Also, if your browser or monitor's zoom settings is set to scale to a non-integer value the pixel art will look crusty.</small>
</ThemedLayout>
